    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-07-06T16:02:44.208Z","headline":"","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_journeesparticulieres-lvmh-savoirfairerever-activity-7479927826754904066-KFp4","text":"It's official: Les Journées Particulières return on October 16, 17 & 18, 2026.\n \nJust like before a match, Antoine Dupont gathers our teams for a talk, turning the energy of the locker room into three days of open doors and shared savoir-faire.\n\n #JourneesParticulieres #LVMH #SavoirFaireRever\n","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_journeesparticulieres-lvmh-savoirfairerever-activity-7479927826754904066-KFp4"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-07-03T10:07:04.306Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-bvlgari-activity-7478751157113470976-kT9a","text":"Bvlgari continues to strengthen its presence in Japan with the opening of its new Shinsaibashi flagship store in Osaka, a space where the Maison's Roman heritage meets Japanese craftsmanship.\n\nReferences to the Serpenti universe run throughout the boutique, from a washi-inspired façade punctuated by the Maison's eight-pointed star to interiors combining Italian marble, travertine and textiles from Kyoto weaving house Hosoo.\n\nThe space also features bespoke artworks created for the location, inspired by the ties between Rome and Osaka.\n\n#LVMH #Bvlgari","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-bvlgari-activity-7478751157113470976-kT9a"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-07-01T15:47:47.343Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-celine-celiness27-activity-7478112125694132224-jFz-","text":"On Sunday June 28th, CELINE presented the Men’s Printemps/été 2027 collection at the Tennis Club de Paris.\n\nThe collection is built around the idea of packing light, making do with a few great things: tailoring, heirloom pieces and good-time shirts.\n\n#LVMH #Celine #CelineSS27","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-celine-celiness27-activity-7478112125694132224-jFz-"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-07-01T15:04:55.212Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-domp%C3%A9rignon-activity-7478101337403068417-i5z1","text":"With the event Révélations, Dom Pérignon opens a window onto the inspirations, artistic dialogues and craftsmanship that shape the Maison.\n \nAt the heart of the 2026 edition was the presentation of Dom Pérignon Vintage 2018, the first vintage crafted entirely under the direction of Chef de Cave Vincent Chaperon. Born from an exceptionally generous year in Champagne, the wine expresses a remarkable sense of harmony and fullness, reflecting the balance that lies at the heart of every Dom Pérignon creation.\n \nThe theme of this year’s edition, “Place”, explores the profound influence of terroir, landscape and environment on the creation of a wine.\n \nConceived as an immersive expression of this theme and the Maison’s universe, the evening unfolded through House of Gestures, a performance at Bilbao Guggenheim Museum co-created by Tilda Swinton and Olivier Saillard. Inspired by Dom Pérignon, the work explored the dialogue between body, gesture and memory, transforming space into a living landscape shaped by emotion, presence and time.\n\n#LVMH #DomPérignon","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-domp%C3%A9rignon-activity-7478101337403068417-i5z1"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-30T14:30:56.096Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-givenchy-givenchyss27-activity-7477730396827291648-h5C3","text":"GIVENCHY unveils its Men’s Spring-Summer 2027 Collection as a private space. A house within a house.\n\nA triptych of rooms, each dedicated to a different facet of the wardrobe. Givenchy archetypes are highlighted, alongside precious embroidered clothing and personal treasures imbued with meaning and emotion.\n\nThis presentation, taking place at Givenchy’s home at 3, avenue George V, is seen in dialogue with the work of artist Rachel Whiteread.\n\n#LVMH #Givenchy #GivenchySS27","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-givenchy-givenchyss27-activity-7477730396827291648-h5C3"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-30T12:27:48.138Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-diorbeauty-activity-7477699409481285633-yLJX","text":"Parfums Christian Dior celebrates its iconic rose with a new exceptional creation, unveiled as part of Les Récoltes Majeures collection, conceived by Francis Kurkdjian.\n\nAmong the flowers that have shaped the history of Dior, the rose holds a special place. A constant source of inspiration for Christian Dior and a defining presence in the Maison’s fragrance creations.\n\nAt the intersection of floral heritage, olfactory creation and exceptional craftsmanship, this limited edition offers a new interpretation of one of Dior’s most enduring symbols. \n\n#LVMH #DiorBeauty","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-diorbeauty-activity-7477699409481285633-yLJX"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-29T10:05:14.750Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-insead-chaumet-activity-7477301146106134528-LU70","text":"Over the past four months, 124 INSEAD students tackled strategic business and creative challenges for CHAUMET, one of the oldest jewellery houses in the LVMH portfolio, guided by the Maison's Executive Committee: Charles Leung (CEO), Claire Hennequin (Global HR Director), Karine Casabonne (VP International Sales), Marc Join-Lambert (Chief Information Officer) and Raphaël Mingam (CMO), and supported throughout by twelve LVMH–INSEAD Alumni mentors.\n\nThis second edition of the Business Creative Force Programme, part of the LVMH–INSEAD Joint Initiative, brought together MBA, Executive MBA, Master in Management and PhD participants from the Fontainebleau and Singapore campuses. Building on the inaugural edition, it is a format designed to bridge academic rigour with the realities of leading a heritage luxury brand.\n\nA highlight was a masterclass by Charles Leung, CEO of CHAUMET, at the INSEAD Fontainebleau campus, offering participants first-hand insight into leadership and the evolving landscape of fine jewellery.\n\nThe experience culminated in a Final Pitch & Awards Ceremony in Paris, in the presence of Jean-Jacques Guiony, President & CEO of Moët Hennessy, Lily Fang, Dean of Research & Innovation at INSEAD, and Pierre-Julien Bousquet, LVMH Group Global VP Talent Engagement.\n\nA testament to the shared ambition of LVMH and INSEAD: connecting academic excellence with industry leadership to shape the next generation of luxury talent.\n\n#LVMH #INSEAD #CHAUMET #Luxury #Talent #Innovation #Leadership","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-insead-chaumet-activity-7477301146106134528-LU70"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-26T15:37:02.166Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-berluti-activity-7476297480306089984-ifrj","text":"Berluti returns for the third consecutive year to the Simone and Cino Del Duca Foundation, unveiling the inspirations, craftsmanship and creative choices that shape the Maison’s universe.\n \nThis year, the Maison explores the theme of the garden through a journey conceived as a passage from idea to material. From ready-to-wear, footwear and leather goods to restoration and artisanal excellence, each space reveals how emotions, references and craftsmanship come together to create lasting objects. Enriched by a dialogue with The Little Prince, the experience highlights the resonances between Antoine de Saint-Exupéry’s universe and Berluti’s world: a careful observation of nature, respect for living things, and an appreciation for the details that give meaning to objects. The creative journey gradually evolved through an ongoing dialogue with The Little Prince, which will also inspire a limited-edition release to be unveiled later this year.\n \n#LVMH #Berluti","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-berluti-activity-7476297480306089984-ifrj"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-26T12:12:51.142Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-dior-diorsummer27-activity-7476246095749165056-88J4","text":"Christian Dior Couture unveils its Summer 2027 Men’s Show, with music by Fred again.., producer, songwriter, multi-instrumentalist and DJ.\n \nSampling and remixing carve out new meaning for what’s known, transforming the familiar, magnifying the subtle and refreshing character.\nThe Summer 2027 Men’s Collection performs similar sleights of hand: skewing conventions, juxtaposing ideas from different eras and replicating what already exists in unexpected ways.\n \nAn exercise in shifting perspectives, reinvention and the euphoria of recognition.\n \n#LVMH #Dior #DiorSummer27\n\nCredits: FINALE BY ADRIEN DIRAND","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-dior-diorsummer27-activity-7476246095749165056-88J4"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"DiscussionForumPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh"},"datePublished":"2026-06-25T15:36:22.664Z","mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-kenzo-kenzoss27-activity-7475934926735929345-kylT","text":"KENZO Mode unveils its Spring-Summer 2027 Men’s and Women’s Collection, as Artistic Director Nigo returns to Place des Victoires, the historic Parisian square where founder Kenzo Takada opened his legendary flagship boutique in 1976.\n \nFifty years later, the square inspires a collection built around encounters and contrasts. Drawing on the Maison’s archives, Ivy League references, romantic ribbon details and contemporary sportswear codes, Nigo reinterprets the spirit of KENZO through a wardrobe that celebrates individuality, freedom and self-expression.\n \nInspired by Kenzo Takada’s enduring optimism, the collection brings past and present together through craftsmanship, innovation and a shared belief that “le monde est beau.”\n \n#LVMH #Kenzo #KENZOSS27","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/lvmh_lvmh-kenzo-kenzoss27-activity-7475934926735929345-kylT"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"LVMH","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"22, avenue Montaigne","addressLocality":"Paris","postalCode":"75008","addressCountry":"FR"},"description":"LVMH is the world leader in luxury.\n\nA family group founded in 1987 and headed by Chairman and CEO Bernard Arnault, LVMH is now home to 75 iconic Maisons, which embody a distinctive art de vivre blending heritage and modernity. With reported sales of 86.2 billion euros in 2023 and 6000 stores around the world, we are the only group present in all major sectors of the luxury industry: Wines & Spirits, Fashion & Leather Goods, Perfumes & Cosmetics, Watches & Jewelry, Selective Distribution.\n\nOur long-term vision, entrepreneurial spirit and constant search for new solutions set us apart. The success of our Group is only possible thanks to our employees: 213,000 passionate and committed women and men, representing 190 nationalities, work in our studios, workshops, wineries, factories, offices and boutiques all around the world. Their talent and their diversity are our strength.\n\nBeing part of LVMH means being continuously inspired by our heritage, creativity and sense of the collective. We have exceptional stories to share and an unrivalled legacy to pass on to future generations.\n\nBeing part of LVMH means being challenged. We set ambitious paths to excellence by continuously pushing the boundaries, raising our standards and renewing ourselves to ensure the long-term development of our Maisons.\n\nBeing part of LVMH means belonging to one of the world’s most creative and innovative communities. We foster collaborations that enable our people to enrich their knowledge, grow their network and share their passions.\n\nBeing part of LVMH means being supported in an inclusive and diverse workplace, where all voices are heard and each talent is given the means to thrive.\n\nIn 6 different industries, across 81 countries, LVMH and its Maisons are committed to exemplary ethics, social and environmental responsibility. We strive to ensure that our products and the way they are made have positive impact on our entire ecosystem and on our host communities.\n\nAt LVMH, we craft the future.","numberOfEmployees":{"value":151378,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4E0BAQG0ZjiacH285Q/company-logo_200_200/B4EZkPHY7tGcAY-/0/1756895219832/lvmh_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=T-ac3kgsOeFuvrHHDEqdW5FoUFiqGNDovVKu6WiFS5Q","description":"LVMH","@type":"ImageObject"},"sameAs":"http://www.lvmh.com"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
