    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary"><a class="link" href="https://it.linkedin.com/company/bulgari?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Bvlgari</a> continues to strengthen its presence in Japan with the opening of its new Shinsaibashi flagship store in Osaka, a space where the Maison's Roman heritage meets Japanese craftsmanship.

References to the Serpenti universe run throughout the boutique, from a washi-inspired façade punctuated by the Maison's eight-pointed star to interiors combining Italian marble, travertine and textiles from Kyoto weaving house Hosoo.

The space also features bespoke artworks created for the location, inspired by the ties between Rome and Osaka.

