        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary"><a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/givenchy?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>GIVENCHY</a> unveils its Men’s Spring-Summer 2027 Collection as a private space. A house within a house.

A triptych of rooms, each dedicated to a different facet of the wardrobe. Givenchy archetypes are highlighted, alongside precious embroidered clothing and personal treasures imbued with meaning and emotion.

This presentation, taking place at Givenchy’s home at 3, avenue George V, is seen in dialogue with the work of artist Rachel Whiteread.

