  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Over the past four months, 124 <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/school/insead/?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>INSEAD</a> students tackled strategic business and creative challenges for <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/chaumet?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>CHAUMET</a>, one of the oldest jewellery houses in the <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/lvmh?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>LVMH</a> portfolio, guided by the Maison's Executive Committee: Charles Leung (CEO), Claire Hennequin (Global HR Director), Karine Casabonne (VP International Sales), Marc Join-Lambert (Chief Information Officer) and Raphaël Mingam (CMO), and supported throughout by twelve LVMH–INSEAD Alumni mentors.

This second edition of the Business Creative Force Programme, part of the LVMH–INSEAD Joint Initiative, brought together MBA, Executive MBA, Master in Management and PhD participants from the Fontainebleau and Singapore campuses. Building on the inaugural edition, it is a format designed to bridge academic rigour with the realities of leading a heritage luxury brand.

A highlight was a masterclass by Charles Leung, CEO of CHAUMET, at the INSEAD Fontainebleau campus, offering participants first-hand insight into leadership and the evolving landscape of fine jewellery.

The experience culminated in a Final Pitch &amp; Awards Ceremony in Paris, in the presence of Jean-Jacques Guiony, President &amp; CEO of <a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/moethennessy?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Moët Hennessy</a>, Lily Fang, Dean of Research &amp; Innovation at INSEAD, and Pierre-Julien Bousquet, LVMH Group Global VP Talent Engagement.

A testament to the shared ambition of LVMH and INSEAD: connecting academic excellence with industry leadership to shape the next generation of luxury talent.

