  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary"><a class="link" href="https://fr.linkedin.com/company/berluti?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Berluti</a> returns for the third consecutive year to the Simone and Cino Del Duca Foundation, unveiling the inspirations, craftsmanship and creative choices that shape the Maison’s universe.
 
This year, the Maison explores the theme of the garden through a journey conceived as a passage from idea to material. From ready-to-wear, footwear and leather goods to restoration and artisanal excellence, each space reveals how emotions, references and craftsmanship come together to create lasting objects. Enriched by a dialogue with The Little Prince, the experience highlights the resonances between Antoine de Saint-Exupéry’s universe and Berluti’s world: a careful observation of nature, respect for living things, and an appreciation for the details that give meaning to objects. The creative journey gradually evolved through an ongoing dialogue with The Little Prince, which will also inspire a limited-edition release to be unveiled later this year.
 
<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Flvmh&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#LVMH</a> <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fberluti&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#Berluti</a></p>
